From bd2b590d0d6642c0d5403c9ab3f46cf4f1dc6791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:55:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Have ambient carjackings called in and chased down

A carjacker used to drive off and simply expire. Now, a few seconds after
the getaway, the victim calls it in (Config.Ambient.carjackResponse):

- A patrol or convoy car already within reuseRadius of the stolen car takes
  the call: it is detached from its own scene (the rest of a convoy goes
  back to patrolling), lights up and chases. Otherwise one to three
  cruisers are spawned out of view 60-140 m from the car, trailing slots
  vetted the same way a convoy's are, within the maxNearbyCops budget.
- The scene then becomes an ordinary NPC pursuit and ends in the existing
  surrender / bail / crash arrest. A new 'responding' phase holds the chase
  clock until a unit is within 40 m of the suspect, re-gives a chase task
  that lapsed on the way, and after a minute without contact lets the
  suspect get away and sends the units off patrolling.
- One call per carjacking, gated by the chance roll, the shared
  pursuitCooldownSeconds, the victim still standing, the player not wanted
  and the getaway within nearbyRadius. A scene torn down while its units
  were spawning cleans them up instead of leaking them.

spawnPursuit is split into joinChase / addChaser / beginNpcPursuit so both
paths share them, and a pursuit whose chasers all fail to spawn is rolled
back rather than fleeing nobody. promoteEnforcer reuses the new
detachOfficer, advancePursuit's departure tail becomes driveOff, and a
carjack scene is never armed for radar while its units are spawning.
enabled = false leaves carjacks exactly as they were.

